.gradle
.omc

# SUN-980 follow-up: exclude host-side build outputs so the Docker builder
# starts from a pristine tree and re-compiles everything from source. Prior
# incident on prod (2026-04-22): a stale BitzeroMini-1.0.jar left over from
# pre-GitLab-#9 checkouts sat under libs/ on the host. Dockerfile does
# `COPY . /build/` which drags it into the builder. game/Minigame's
# fileTree(dir:'../../libs') picked it up onto classpath. Since BitzeroMini
# has the same bitzero.util.ExtensionUtility class path as
# BitZeroMinigame (the source fork that has sendLogoutOK), the stale jar
# shadowed the source fork and game/Minigame compiled against the wrong
# class → missing sendLogoutOK at runtime.
#
# Excluding these dirs here is defence-in-depth — the builder compiles
# every module from source via `./gradlew build copyRuntimeDeps` regardless
# of what jars happen to sit on the host.
libs/
all-libs/
runtime-libs/
game/*/libs/

# Per-module build outputs on host — equally stale, equally regenerable.
**/build/

# Runtime logs directory — grew to 18 GB on prod and was silently being
# copied into the build context every rebuild (tonight's deploy transferred
# 9+ GB before we caught it). Never needed for build.
logs/
**/logs/

# Stale quarantine dirs left from previous deploys' disaster recovery.
_quarantine_*/
